<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  PyrelandsWeather_BlackRain.xml   RimUtinni: Fire Ecology   2026-09-01
  ============================================================================
  FIRE_ECOLOGY_LOOP_1, unit 2 — wires RSW_FE_BlackRain (RimMandrake: SW —
  Fire Ecology) into the Pyrelands' own weather table at a LOW base share,
  same dictionary-shorthand xpath pattern as PyrelandsWeather_Stage0.xml
  (apply AFTER that file — both are PatchOperationAdd/Replace against the
  same list, load order inside one mod's Patches/ folder is alphabetical,
  "BlackRain" > "Stage0" so this is safe).

  Kept at commonality 1 deliberately — low enough that it almost never rolls
  under ordinary Clear(55)/DryThunderstorm(35) dominance. It does not need a
  bigger base number: WeatherDecider.CurrentWeatherCommonality's existing
  ChanceFactorRainOnFire (15x, RimSage, WeatherDecider.cs:185) only fires
  while map.fireWatcher.LargeFireDangerPresent is true, and at that moment
  Black Rain is the ONLY rainRate>0.1 weather left in this table (Stage 0
  removed all the others) — so it goes from "almost never" to "effectively
  the next roll" exactly when a big fire is burning, and stays "almost
  never" the rest of the time. See BlackRain.xml's own header for the full
  mechanism citation.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>More Vanilla Biomes</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="ZBiome_Grasslands"]/baseWeatherCommonalities</xpath>
          <value>
            <RSW_FE_BlackRain>1</RSW_FE_BlackRain>
          </value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
